@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "What is CI/CD?";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Continuous Integration (CI) and Continuous Deployment (CD) are key DevOps practices that help teams **automate, test, and deploy software efficiently**. Azure DevOps provides robust CI/CD pipelines to streamline software delivery.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>What is Continuous Integration (CI)?</h2>
        <p>Continuous Integration (CI) is a software development practice where **developers regularly merge their code changes** into a shared repository. Each integration is verified by automated builds and tests to detect and fix issues early.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Developers commit code frequently to version control (e.g., Git, Azure Repos).</li>
            <li>Automated builds and tests ensure code quality.</li>
            <li>Detects integration issues early, reducing debugging time.</li>
            <li>Improves collaboration across development teams.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/continuous-integration.png" alt="Continuous Integration Process" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Continuous Integration (CI) process</small></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>CI Workflow in Azure DevOps</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>Developer pushes code to **Azure Repos**.</li>
                <li>Azure Pipelines triggers an **automated build**.</li>
                <li>Unit and integration tests are executed.</li>
                <li>Build artifacts are generated for deployment.</li>
                <li>Any failed tests trigger alerts for immediate action.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>What is Continuous Deployment (CD)?</h2>
        <p>Continuous Deployment (CD) automates the release of software to production **after passing all automated tests**. It ensures that new features and bug fixes are delivered to users quickly and reliably.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Code changes are automatically deployed to staging and production.</li>
            <li>Reduces manual intervention and human errors.</li>
            <li>Allows teams to release new features faster.</li>
            <li>Enables A/B testing and feature toggles for gradual rollouts.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>CD Workflow in Azure DevOps</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>CI process completes successfully.</li>
                <li>Deployment pipelines deploy the build artifacts.</li>
                <li>Infrastructure provisioning happens automatically.</li>
                <li>Automated smoke tests verify deployment integrity.</li>
                <li>Application is released to production users.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/continuous-deployment.png" alt="Continuous Deployment Process" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Continuous Deployment (CD) process</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Benefits of CI/CD</h2>
        <p>Implementing CI/CD pipelines offers numerous advantages:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Faster Releases:</strong> Automates software delivery, reducing time-to-market.</li>
            <li><strong>Higher Code Quality:</strong> Continuous testing catches defects early.</li>
            <li><strong>Increased Collaboration:</strong> Developers work seamlessly with operations teams.</li>
            <li><strong>Reliability:</strong> Reduces deployment failures and improves rollback mechanisms.</li>
            <li><strong>Scalability:</strong> Easily integrates with cloud services like Azure.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            CI/CD pipelines streamline the software development lifecycle by **automating builds, tests, and deployments**. Azure DevOps provides powerful tools to implement CI/CD, ensuring faster and more reliable software releases.
        </p>
        <p>
            The next step is to explore **Creating & Configuring Build Pipelines in Azure DevOps**.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-end mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("CreatingConfiguringBuildPipelines", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Next: Creating & Configuring Build Pipelines &rarr;</a>
    </div>
</div>
